      "id": "aud-m3-tbs4-ex1",
      "title": "Evidence received",
      "html": "<p>A customer did not respond to a positive request. A response was forwarded through management from an unverified address. Goods counted include a clearly identified consignment from another company. A bank confirmation agrees to the bank statement, but the book reconciliation contains unusual old transfers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "aud-m3-tbs4-ex2",
      "title": "Audit approach",
      "html": "<p>Evaluate each item’s reliability and assertion implications. No alternative procedure has yet been performed, and the balances are material.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Follow-up for the nonresponse</h3><p>A positive request requires appropriate evidence rather than silence.</p><h3>Follow-up for the forwarded response</h3><p>Reliability must be established in the circumstances.</p><h3>Assertion implicated by the consignment</h3><p>Physical custody does not establish ownership.</p><h3>Follow-up for old bank transfers</h3><p>Unusual reconciling items can affect the book cash balance and cutoff.</p>"
